# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# earnings-themes
#
# Tracked deliberately -- do NOT add these here:
#   uv.lock                       one reviewed workspace lockfile (AGENTS.md)
#   config/ prompts/ codebooks/   versioned settings, prompts, codebooks
#   tests/fixtures/               small, redistributable fixtures only
#
# ORDERING MATTERS: git applies the LAST matching pattern. The credentials
# block is deliberately last so no later negation can re-admit a secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Data artifacts --------------------------------------------------------
# AGENTS.md layout: data/{raw,canonical,processed,runs} are ignored by Git.
# Use `data/*` rather than `data/` so a directory skeleton can be re-admitted
# later with a negation, e.g. !data/raw/.gitkeep
data/*

# Large downloads and generated outputs wherever they land.
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.feather
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.zip
*.gz
*.tar
*.warc

# Small, redistributable fixtures are the documented exception.
!tests/fixtures/**

# --- Logs, traces, run outputs ---------------------------------------------
# AGENTS.md: keep secrets and restricted full text out of logs/traces.
*.log
logs/
traces/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Environments ----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Tooling caches --------------------------------------------------------
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytype/
.dmypy.json
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.hypothesis/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Editors and OS --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- Credentials and contact configuration ---------------------------------
# MUST REMAIN THE LAST BLOCK. AGENTS.md: the SEC User-Agent contact is
# "configured outside committed code"; keep credentials, secrets, and contact
# config out of Git. These rules override the fixture negation above.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/**/*.local.*
config/secrets/
.secrets/
secrets.toml
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
